{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.WronskianHeight","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WronskianHeight","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.MvGenWronskian","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.MvPolynomialHeight","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Bounds","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.BigOperators"],"declarations":36,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_pderiv_iterate_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_pderiv_iterate_le","kind":"theorem","line":870,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L870-L907","doc":"**§7's coefficient bound in one variable, sharp.**\n\n    |coeff n (∂ⱼ^k g)| ≤ k! · 2^d · B      whenever  degreeOf j g ≤ d  and  |coeff · g| ≤ B\n\nCompare `abs_coeff_pderivList_le`, which gives `d^k·B`.  The two agree in shape only when `k` is\nsmall: the sharp form separates `k!` — the **whole** discrepancy with Mahler's divided\nderivative — and leaves a binomial, which `Nat.choose_le_two_pow` sends to `2^d`.  That `2^d` is\n§7's `2^{r_h}`, and it is what makes §12's budget `2^{(2m+1)ρ₁}` come out.\n\n⚠ Sharp in `k`, and that is the point: at `k ≈ d` the crude bound is `d^d` where this is\n`k!·2^d ≈ (d/e)^d·2^d`. Neither dominates for all `k`, but only this one has the factorial\n*visible*, so only this one lets the divided derivative be recovered by dividing it out. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_divided_wronskian_budget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_divided_wronskian_budget","kind":"theorem","line":828,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L828-L868","doc":"**§12's height estimate and §11's clause 4, joined.**\n\nEverything §13's descent needs from the height theory, in the shape `rothGammaFull_descend`\nconsumes it: an integral `W` with `det = C c · W`, `c > 0`, and\n\n    |coeff W| ≤ 2^{(2n+3)·(r₀·d_first)} · a^{r₀}\n\nwhich is `b ≤ 2^{c'}·a^{r₀}` with `c' = (2n+3)·(r₀·d_first)` — clause 4 exactly.\n\nThe three inputs are the degree bound, the height bound `a`, and the ordering facts\n`r₀ ≤ d_last + 1` (Mahler's `n ≤ r_m + 1`), `Σd ≤ (n+1)·d_first` and `d_last ≤ d_first`.  `S` is\ntaken to be `2^{Σd}` itself, which `card_support_le_two_pow_sum` supplies and `height_budget`\naccepts with `le_rfl`.\n\n⚠ `c > 0` rather than `c ≠ 0` — it is a product of factorials, and the sign is free.  The\nconsumers only need non-vanishing (`index_C_mul`), but positivity is what the proof produces\nand there is no reason to weaken it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.height_budget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.height_budget","kind":"theorem","line":774,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L774-L826","doc":"**§12's budget closes** — and by exactly one factor of `r₀·d_first`.\n\n`exists_divided_wronskian` gives `|coeff W| ≤ r₀!·S^{r₀}·(2^{Σd}·a)^{r₀}`.  §11's clause 4 wants\n`b ≤ 2^c·a^{r₀}` with `c ≤ (2m+1)·(r₀·d_first)` — which is `rothGammaFull_descend`'s\n`(2n+3)·(r₀·d (o.symm 0))` at `m = n + 1`.  The two meet:\n\n    S^{r₀} ≤ 2^{r₀Σd},   (2^{Σd}·a)^{r₀} = 2^{r₀Σd}·a^{r₀},   so   b ≤ r₀!·2^{2r₀Σd}·a^{r₀}\n    Σd ≤ (n+1)·d_first                      gives  2r₀Σd ≤ (2n+2)·r₀·d_first\n    r₀! ≤ r₀^{r₀} ≤ (d_last+1)^{r₀} ≤ 2^{r₀·d_first}\n\nand `(2n+2) + 1 = 2n+3`.  So the factorial is what the last unit of the budget pays for, and\nthere is nothing else to spend it on — §12's `2^{2n(r₁+…+r_m)}·n!·a^n` names both terms.\n\n⚠ `d_last + 1 ≤ 2^{d_first}` is the only place the growth ordering is used, and it is used only\nthrough `d_last ≤ d_first`.  The `+1` survives because `k + 1 ≤ 2^k`, not because of any\nestimate on the degrees' ratio — so a *degenerate* growth constant would not break this step,\nonly the row cost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_support_le_two_pow_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_support_le_two_pow_sum","kind":"theorem","line":766,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L766-L772","doc":"**`S := 2^{Σd}` serves both lemmas** — `exists_divided_wronskian`'s `hS` and\n`height_budget`'s `hS`, with `hS1 : 1 ≤ S` free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.prod_succ_le_two_pow_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.prod_succ_le_two_pow_sum","kind":"theorem","line":759,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L759-L764","doc":"**The box, in the budget's currency.**  `∏ (d h + 1) ≤ 2^{Σ d h}`, term by term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_support_le_prod_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_support_le_prod_succ","kind":"theorem","line":731,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L731-L757","doc":"**A polynomial's support is bounded by the box its degrees cut out.**\n\nStated over an arbitrary coefficient semiring: nothing in the proof is arithmetic, it is a\nstatement about which multi-indices can occur.  It was written against `ℤ` for §12's budget and\ngeneralised when Roth's theorem's step 2 needed the same count over `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_divided_wronskian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_divided_wronskian","kind":"theorem","line":644,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L644-L722","doc":"**§12's height estimate, for the divided-derivative Wronskian.**\n\nThe determinant of `∂^{Dx i ⊞ Dy j} P` is `C·W` with `W` **integral** and\n\n    |coeff n W| ≤ r! · S^r · (2^{Σ_h d_h} · B)^r\n\nWith `S ≤ ∏_h (d_h + 1) ≤ 2^{Σ_h d_h}` that reads `r!·2^{2r·Σ_h d_h}·B^r` — **§12's\n`b = 2^{2n(r₁+…+r_m)}·n!·a^n`, exactly.**\n\n`W` is Mahler's `W`: the same determinant built from divided derivatives.  Its index is the\ndeterminant's (`index_C_mul`), so nothing the index calculus proves is lost, and its height is\nsmaller by the `C` that correction twenty-one identified — `2^{Θ(r² log r)}`, which §12's budget\nhas no room for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listFac_append_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listFac_append_map","kind":"theorem","line":627,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L627-L642","doc":"**`Fac` splits across the `x`/`y` join** — here as an *equality*, because the two lists live\nin disjoint variables.\n\n`listFac_mul_dvd_listFac_append` gives only divisibility and needs no disjointness; the size side\nneeds the equality, and the separated family supplies it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listIdx_map_inr_apply_inl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listIdx_map_inr_apply_inl","kind":"theorem","line":619,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L619-L625","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listIdx_map_inl_apply_inr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listIdx_map_inl_apply_inr","kind":"theorem","line":611,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L611-L617","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_det_le'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_det_le'","kind":"theorem","line":571,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L571-L609","doc":"**`abs_coeff_det_le` with a row-times-column per-entry bound.**\n\n    |coeff n (det M)| ≤ (#ι)! · S^{#ι} · (∏ aᵢ)(∏ bⱼ)      when  |coeff · (M i j)| ≤ aᵢ·bⱼ\n\nThe mirror of `C_dvd_det_of_dvd_entries` on the size side, and for the same reason: every\npermutation term picks one entry per row and one per column, so `∏_i a_{p i}·b_i` is\n`(∏a)(∏b)` independently of `p`.\n\nTogether the two say that a determinant whose entries carry a factorised row/column constant\nis *that constant* times something both integral and small — which is exactly the relationship\nbetween this arc's `mvGenWronskian` and Mahler's `W`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_prod_le'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_prod_le'","kind":"theorem","line":534,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L534-L569","doc":"**`abs_coeff_prod_le` with per-factor bounds.**\n\n`|coeff n (∏ Fᵢ)| ≤ S^{#s} · ∏ βᵢ` when `|coeff · Fᵢ| ≤ βᵢ`.  The uniform version is the case\n`βᵢ ≡ B`; the point of the general one is that a *factorised* per-entry bound survives the\ndeterminant expansion, which a uniform one cannot express.\n\n⚠ Unlike `abs_coeff_prod_le`, this needs **no `1 ≤ S`** — the empty product is `1` and the bound\nis `S^0·1 = 1`, so nothing forces `S` up.  A first draft carried `1 ≤ S`, copied from the uniform\nversion's signature without checking; the linter caught it.  That is the sixth unused hypothesis\nthis arc has acquired by transcribing a proof *route* rather than the proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.C_listFac_dvd_det_sepFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.C_listFac_dvd_det_sepFamily","kind":"theorem","line":506,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L506-L532","doc":"**§7's constant divides the separated family's determinant.**\n\n    (∏_i Fac(Dx i)) · (∏_j Fac(Dy j))  ∣  det (∂^{Dx i ⊞ Dy j} P)\n\nso the quotient — Mahler's `W`, built from divided derivatives — is an **integral** polynomial.\nThat quotient is the object §12 measures, its index is the same (`index_C_mul`: scaling does not\nmove the index), and its height is `2^{Θ(n² log n)}` smaller, which is exactly the gap correction\ntwenty-one identified between this arc's `mvGenWronskian` and Mahler's `W`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.C_dvd_det_of_dvd_entries","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.C_dvd_det_of_dvd_entries","kind":"theorem","line":481,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L481-L504","doc":"**A row/column-factorising divisor of every entry divides the determinant.**\n\nIf `C (a i · b j)` divides entry `(i,j)`, then `C ((∏ a)·(∏ b))` divides `det` — because every\npermutation term picks one entry per row and one per column, so `∏_i a i · b (σ i)` is\n`(∏ a)(∏ b)` **independently of `σ`**.\n\nThis is what makes correction twenty-one's repair possible at all: the discrepancy between `∂^l`\nand Mahler's `Δ^l` is a row factor times a column factor, and a determinant is exactly the\nshape that turns such a thing into a single scalar. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listFac_mul_dvd_listFac_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listFac_mul_dvd_listFac_append","kind":"theorem","line":468,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L468-L479","doc":"**The row and column factorials divide the combined one.**\n\n`m!·n! ∣ (m+n)!` per variable, so `Fac(l₁)·Fac(l₂) ∣ Fac(l₁ ++ l₂)`.  ⚠ No disjointness of the\ntwo lists' variables is needed — that is the point of using divisibility rather than the\nequality that *would* need it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listIdx_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listIdx_append","kind":"theorem","line":462,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L462-L466","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_pderivList_le'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_pderivList_le'","kind":"theorem","line":430,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L430-L460","doc":"**§7's coefficient bound for `∂^l`** — the replacement for `abs_coeff_pderivList_le`.\n\n    |coeff n (∂^l g)| ≤ (∏_h t_h!) · 2^{Σ_h d_h} · B\n\nAgainst the old `d^{|l|}·B`, this separates the factorial and leaves §7's `2^{Σ r_h}`.  Dividing\nthrough by `∏_h t_h!` — legitimate by `listFac_dvd_coeff_pderivList` — gives the divided\nderivative's bound, which is the one §12's budget is calibrated for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listFac_dvd_coeff_pderivList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listFac_dvd_coeff_pderivList","kind":"theorem","line":420,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L420-L428","doc":"**The factorial divides every coefficient of `∂^l g`.**\n\nSo `∂^l = Fac(l)·(divided derivative)` at the level of coefficients, which is precisely the\nstatement that Mahler's `Δ` is integral and this arc's `∂^l` is `Fac(l)` times it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listFactor_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listFactor_le","kind":"theorem","line":403,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L403-L418","doc":"**§7's bound, for a list of variables.**\n\n    listFactor l n ≤ (∏_h t_h!) · 2^{Σ_h d_h}      whenever  n_h + t_h ≤ d_h\n\nThe `2^{Σ_h d_h}` is §7's `2^{r₁+…+r_m}` exactly — its source is `binom(N,k) ≤ 2^N`, which is\nthe same inequality Mahler writes as `binom(r,j) ≤ Σ_j binom(r,j) = 2^r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listFac_dvd_listFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listFac_dvd_listFactor","kind":"theorem","line":396,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L396-L401","doc":"**The factorial part divides.**  This is what makes the divided derivative *integral*, and\nhence what lets `det` be divided by `(∏_i (Dx i)!)(∏_j (Dy j)!)` and stay in `ℤ[x]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listFactor_eq_factorial_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listFactor_eq_factorial_mul","kind":"theorem","line":380,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L380-L394","doc":"**`listFactor` factors as `Fac(l)·Binom`** — the whole content of correction twenty-one, in\none equation.\n\n    listFactor l n = (∏_h t_h!) · (∏_h binom(n_h + t_h, t_h)),    t = listIdx l\n\nThe left factor is the discrepancy with Mahler's divided derivative; the right is what §7 bounds\nby `2^{Σ r_h}`.  Everything else follows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listFactor_eq_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listFactor_eq_prod","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L337-L378","doc":"**`listFactor` in closed form**, as a product over the variables.\n\n    listFactor l n = ∏_h ∏_{i<t_h} (n_h + 1 + i),   t = listIdx l\n\n⚠ The interleaving is invisible: `∂ⱼ` applied when `n` has already been shifted by `e_h` for\n`h ≠ j` still sees the same `n_j`, so the factors for each variable are consecutive regardless\nof the order the list interleaves them.  That is why a *list* factor equals a *multiset* one.\n\n`s` is any `Finset` containing the list's variables — no `Fintype σ` needed, and the caller\npicks whatever ambient finset is convenient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listFactor_replicate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listFactor_replicate","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L323-L335","doc":"**`listFactor` at a single variable** agrees with `coeff_pderiv_iterate`'s product.\n\nThe bridge that lets the one-variable bound be reused: `∂ⱼ^k` is `∂^l` for the constant list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.coeff_pderivList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.coeff_pderivList","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L304-L321","doc":"**The coefficient of an iterated partial derivative along a list, exactly.**\n\n    coeff n (∂^l g) = listFactor l n · coeff (n + listIdx l) g\n\nThe generalisation of `coeff_pderiv_iterate` from one variable to a list, and the handle the\nrest of correction twenty-one hangs on: both the divisibility `Fac(l) ∣ listFactor l n` and the\nbound `listFactor l n ≤ Fac(l)·2^{Σ d_h}` are statements about `listFactor` alone, with the\npolynomial gone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listFactor_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listFactor_cons","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L301-L302","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listFactor_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listFactor_nil","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L299-L299","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listFactor","kind":"def","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L288-L297","doc":"The integer `∂^l` multiplies the coefficient at `n` by.\n\nDefined by the recursion `∂ⱼ` itself performs — `coeff n (∂ⱼ f) = (nⱼ+1)·coeff (n+eⱼ) f` — so\n`coeff_pderivList` below is an immediate induction.  In closed form it is\n`∏_h (n_h + t_h)!/(n_h)!` with `t = listIdx l`, hence `Fac(l)·∏_h binom(n_h+t_h, t_h)` where\n`Fac(l) = ∏_h (t_h)!`; that factorisation is what correction twenty-one needs and is **not yet\nproved** — see the note below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listIdx_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listIdx_cons","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L285-L286","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listIdx_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listIdx_nil","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L283-L283","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.listIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.listIdx","kind":"def","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L278-L281","doc":"The multi-index a list of variables differentiates by: `listIdx [x,y,x] = 2·e_x + e_y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.coeff_pderiv_iterate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.coeff_pderiv_iterate","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L250-L276","doc":"**The coefficient of an iterated partial derivative**, exactly:\n\n    coeff n (∂ⱼ^k g) = (n_j + 1)(n_j + 2)⋯(n_j + k) · coeff (n + k·eⱼ) g\n\nThe product is `k!·binom(n_j + k, k)`.  **The `k!` is exactly what separates `∂^k` from the\ndivided derivative**, and `binom(n_j+k, k) ≤ 2^{n_j+k}` is §7's `2^r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_det_sepFamily_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_det_sepFamily_le","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L184-L215","doc":"**The height bound made uniform in the family.**\n\n`abs_coeff_det_pderivList_le` needs a bound `L` on the operator lists' lengths.  For the\nfamily the induction step actually forms — `D i j = (Dx i)⊞(Dy j)` with `Dx`, `Dy` of bounded\norder — that bound is available from `r` alone: `|Dx i| ≤ i < r` and `|Dy j| ≤ j < r`, so every\nentry's list has length at most `2r`.\n\n⚠ This is what makes `hres` assemblable.  `hres` quantifies over the families realising a\nseparated representation, so its auxiliary data — the height bound `B` in particular — has to\nbe chosen **before** the family is known.  A bound depending on the individual `D i j` would\nbe useless there; one depending only on `r` and `P` is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_det_pderivList_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_det_pderivList_le","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L158-L181","doc":"**`H(det (∂_{D i j} P)) ≤ r! · (S · (d^L · B))^r`.**\n\nThe height counterpart of `sum_max_le_index_det`, for the matrix Mahler §13 actually forms:\none operator list per *entry*, all applied to a single `P`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_mvGenWronskian_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_mvGenWronskian_le","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L85-L125","doc":"**The height of a generalized Wronskian:**\n\n    H(mvGenWronskian D f)  ≤  m! · (S · (d^L · B))^m\n\nfor `f : Fin m → MvPolynomial σ ℤ` whose supports have size at most `S`, whose degrees in\nevery variable are at most `d`, and whose heights are at most `B`, with each operator list\n`D i` of length at most `L`.\n\nThis is the composite the arc had been assembling in pieces.  Each matrix entry is\n`pderivList (D i) (f j)`, so `abs_coeff_pderivList_le` bounds its height by `d^{|D i|}·B ≤ d^L·B`\nand `card_support_pderivList_le` keeps its support at `S`; `abs_coeff_det_le` then does the\nLeibniz expansion.\n\nThe hypotheses `1 ≤ S`, `1 ≤ d`, `0 ≤ B` are not restrictive — any bound can be raised to meet\nthem — and they are what let the result be stated as a clean power rather than a product of\nper-index factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_pderivList_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_pderivList_le","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L59-L83","doc":"**`H(pderivList l g) ≤ d^{|l|} · H(g)`** when every `degreeOf j g ≤ d`.\n\nEach step costs one factor `d`, and crucially the *same* `d` works at every step: `degreeOf`\ndoes not grow under differentiation, so the degree bound assumed for `g` is inherited by every\nintermediate derivative.  Without that the bound would degrade along the list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_support_pderivList_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_support_pderivList_le","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianHeight.lean#L49-L57","doc":"**Iterated differentiation does not enlarge the support.**  The list form of\n`card_support_pderiv_le`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}